<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Notation</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Vector operations</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Take vectors <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}^{\top}{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}^{\top}{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>: vector inner-product</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}{\bm{y}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}{\bm{y}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>: vector outer-product</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Operators</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\odot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\odot</annotation></semantics></math>: Hadamard product</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\oplus" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊕</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\oplus</annotation></semantics></math>: Concatenation</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Implementation Details</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Most of the experimental details are included across sections <a href="#S2" title="2 Background &amp; Related Works ‣ Paying Attention to Hybrid Attention: Untangling the Issues with Conversion Methods" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>- <a href="#S4" title="4 Methods &amp; Results ‣ Paying Attention to Hybrid Attention: Untangling the Issues with Conversion Methods" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Any details which aren’t explicitly mentioned either in theses sections or this one are aligned with related works and clearly mentioned as such.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.1 </span>Weights Initialisation</h4>

<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Linear projections, as in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, were initialised as the identity, following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2024b)</a></cite>, with added Gaussian-sampled noise (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>) using a seed-based generator to ensure the same initialisation across all runs.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Extended Related Works</h3>

<figure id="A1.T5" class="ltx_table">
